  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlParseNCNameComplex",
    "file": "libxml2/parser.c",
    "description": "xmlParseNCNameComplex computes a name length by scanning with CUR_CHAR/NEXTL but then passes (BASE_PTR + startPosition, len) directly to xmlDictLookup without ensuring that len bytes are actually available in the current input buffer. With malformed imported stylesheet data (including invalid multibyte bytes), this can produce an overlarge len relative to the real remaining buffer, so xmlDictAddString memcpy reads past the source buffer, causing the ASan global-buffer-overflow (read past xmlIsPubidChar_tab). Crash manifests in xmlDictAddString, but root cause is missing bounds validation in xmlParseNCNameComplex before dictionary lookup/copy.",
    "conditions": "In the xslt harness, the top stylesheet contains xsl:import href=\"article.xsl\", so libxslt loads attacker-controlled secondary content via xsltParseStylesheetImport -> xsltDocDefaultLoaderFunc -> xmlParseDocument. The imported document must drive parser.c down the complex NCName path (non-ASCII/invalid bytes) and create a start-tag/name parse where computed len exceeds actually available bytes in the parser input window; then xmlDictLookup/xmlDictAddString copies len bytes from that pointer and over-reads into adjacent global data, triggering the reported global-buffer-overflow."
  },
